Dear Colleagues,

                         



                            Global Warming Conference/Seminar Invitation



You are cordially invited to the 3rd Working Group on Global Warming & Expo 10

international Conference/Seminar and Recruitment Programme.

This forum is affiliated by an international Advisory Board, United Nations

Organization (UN)  in collaboration with many other profound Organizations and

companies in (UK) United Kingdom.



The Conference will comprise the following :-



* Seminar Presentations on Global Warming & Climate Change.

* Seminar Presentations & Lectures on World Poverty Alleviation.

* Seminar Presentations & Lectures on (HSE) Regulations in Science & Technology.

* Seminar Presentations & Lectures on Business Empowerment.

* Scholarship & Financial Support Programme for Undergraduate  & Postgraduate

Students.

* Recruitment of Trainees & Professionals of various fields into different

positions in different Companies & Organizations in UK.



WGGW Conference & Expo 10 will include invited and refereed papers from

academics, consultants, entrepreneurs, investors, technology providers,

designers, sustainability, environment and Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR)

managers as well as other business functions. The event will be a unique

learning experience, networking space and an opportunity to think. Delegates

will come globally from companies, entrepreneurs, as well as academia,

government and non-governmental organizations (NGOs)



We also want to use this opportunity to announce the call for papers, as WGGW

Conference & Expo 10 will welcome conceptual and research-based papers covering

sustainable innovation, technology, product and service design and development.

Papers focused on low carbon solutions and sustainable innovation related to the

following topics are particularly welcomed:



&#65533; Global Warming and Climate Change and the Oceans

&#65533; Sustainable Environment, Health and Development

&#65533; Remote Sensing and Global Surveillance

&#65533; Water Resources Management

&#65533; Carbon & GHG Management

&#65533; Extreme Events and Impacts Assessment

&#65533; Greenhouse Gas & Ecosystems

&#65533; Human Health In a Changing Climate

&#65533; Agricultural and Forestry Resources Management

&#65533; Clean Energy Technology

&#65533; Low GHG Transportation

&#65533; Education: Global Change & Sustainable Development

&#65533; Case studies

&#65533; (HSE) Regulations in Science & Technology

&#65533; World Poverty alleviation



We also want to bring to your notice that the following expenses would be

covered through our access fund (WGGW) to ensure your effective participation in

this upcoming conference/Seminar:-



* Air ticket to and fro to London, Per Diem

* Visa cost and Travel insurance to the Conference/Seminar



Date: 16th &#65533; 21th May,2011

Time: 10am - 5pm Daily.

Venue: (Conference Hall) Mayfair Hotel UK, 26 Park Lane London, W1K 1BE, United

Kingdom.





